~ start
Leona and Pearl meet at a Sunday market
Leona: Pearl! Sugar, over here!
Pearl: Leona.
Leona: Is that a clipboard? 
Pearl: Market list, categorized by vendor location with optimized routes.
Leona: You made me one too.
Pearl: Efficiently benefits both parties.
Leona: How thoughtful, thank you. Pearl, do you smell that? Those are fresh sea lily candles, and I have been meaning to get one since last Sunday.
Pearl: That stall isn’t on route until section C
Leona: Baby, my nose does not run on a schedule. You got to go with the flow sometimes. Are you looking for someone who is as precise as you? 
Pearl: The opposite, actually.
Leona: Honey, you’ll have to learn how to compromise with them. If you want someone who is the opposite of you, you will have to act like they’re welcomed. I appreciate the clipboard, but let's throw it away for today and go wherever the current takes us. 
Pearl and Leona browse the endless rows of vendors aimlessly to their hearts contents 
Pearl: This is why I need a partner who is the opposite of me. This was fun.
Leona: It really was fun and I think you’re going to make someone very very happy one day.
Pearl: But not with you.
Leona: Sorry sugar but you saw me out there. I enjoy the freedom of life more than anything. I can’t be tied down to a partner, even if they’re as lovely as you.
Pearl: I understand. Thank you for showing me how to live a little freely.
After date
Leona: Pearl was great company, but darlin’ I always enjoy things at my own pace and schedule. I’m already where I want to be. 
+5 satisfaction. Fulfilled 
Pearl: Leona fit me well, but she isn’t looking for a partner anymore.
+0 satisfaction. Neither heartbroken, neither fulfilled 
